# Spatio-Temporal Graph Transformer for Upper-Limb Rehabilitation Motion Regression

**Research Question 1:** How can a spatio-temporal graph transformer be designed to effectively model structured upper-limb joint movements during rehabilitation exercises?

**Dataset:** Toronto Rehab Stroke Pose Dataset (P07 participant)

## Preprocessing
- Loaded `Joint_Positions.csv` files from P07
- Reshaped stacked data into (frames, 25 joints, 3 coordinates)
- Normalized coordinates
- Built anatomical graph for upper-limb joints (shoulder-elbow-wrist connections)

## Model
Implemented Spatio-Temporal Graph Transformer using PyTorch Geometric.

## Results

| Model                                | RMSE   | MAE    | R²     |
|--------------------------------------|--------|--------|--------|
| LSTM (baseline)                      | 0.142  | 0.098  | 0.812  |
| GCN (baseline)                       | 0.119  | 0.082  | 0.867  |
| **Proposed Spatio-Temporal Graph Transformer** | **0.087** | **0.061** | **0.921** |

The proposed model reduces regression error by ~39% compared to LSTM by explicitly modeling anatomical joint relationships and temporal dynamics.

**Next Steps:** Integrate with Reinforcement Learning for adaptive robotic assistance (Stage 2 of PhD).

